    "problem_statement": "URL scheme stripping broken for URLs without scheme\n\nWhen using furl with URLs that don't have a scheme, the `strip_scheme` function incorrectly removes characters from the beginning of the URL.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom furl import furl\n\n# URLs without schemes get mangled\nf = furl.furl('www.example.com/path')\nprint(f.url)  # Expected: 'www.example.com/path', but gets mangled\n\nf = furl.furl('127.0.0.1:8080/api')\nprint(f.url)  # Expected: '127.0.0.1:8080/api', but gets mangled\n\nf = furl.furl('localhost/test')\nprint(f.url)  # Expected: 'localhost/test', but gets mangled\n```\n\nThe issue appears when parsing URLs that don't start with a scheme like `http://` or `https://`. The URL gets incorrectly processed and characters are stripped from the beginning."
